The browser build matches Vite's actual package graph in both directions against
ThirdPartyNotices/npm-browser-packages.json, then generates
dist/ThirdPartyNotices/npm-browser-dependencies.txt from those installed package roots and their
installed runtime dependency closure. This conservatively covers dependencies incorporated into
prebundled package entry points that Vite sees as one module root. The same generated text appears
in Settings > Legal. The server build likewise checks its actual external
imports against the server category and emits both an external-package manifest and installed
runtime-closure legal text under dist-server/ThirdPartyNotices/. A dependency graph or NOTICE list
that drifts in either direction fails the build.

The installed livekit-client package currently has a root Apache-2.0 LICENSE and no root NOTICE;
the generated browser report carries exactly those installed legal files. If a later installed
version adds a NOTICE, the generator includes it automatically. Apache-2.0 section 4(d) applies
when the particular upstream work being distributed includes such a NOTICE.

