The texture, skybox, and prop generation features call hosted models through the fal.ai API using a
key you supply. The key is sent with that one call and is never stored or logged by the service; the
browser keeps it in its own localStorage on your machine so you need not re-enter it (docs/033). The models are
operated by fal and its model providers under their own terms; what those terms permit you to do
with a generated image or mesh is between you and them. src/core/paint/fal-models.ts names every
endpoint the proxy will call.

tools/generate-terrain/ builds height maps from two public sources it queries at run time:

    USGS 3D Elevation Program (3DEP) lidar     public domain (a United States Government work)
      https://www.usgs.gov/3d-elevation-program
    OpenStreetMap ski-piste geometry           Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0
      © OpenStreetMap contributors — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

    OSM data is used only to choose which square of terrain to fetch; the height maps themselves are
    USGS lidar and are not a derivative database. Generated OSM data remains under ODbL, and static map
    images are Produced Works that display the required attribution. Queries go through the volunteer-run
    Overpass API — observe its usage policy.

